-- title:
--   Original source X-minus-jumps stopped C2 Gaussian finite mesh expected Ito drift with one-half sigma squared
-- statement:
--   For the exact original X source, subtract its explicitly assumed small- and large-jump components and drift to obtain the Gaussian continuous residual M. A finite sum of stopped source-specific C2 first- and second-derivative weighted Gaussian increments has expectation exactly sigma squared over two times the sum of duration-weighted expected Hessians; each summand is integrable. The same-space zero-jump Lévy Gaussian witness and source decomposition are explicit hypotheses.
-- source:
--   Consequence of remotely Proved finite-mesh Gaussian C2 Ito expectation theorem on the same source, transferred algebraically to M = X - drift - jump components.

